Package: freshroot
Architecture: all
Depends: btrfs-progs, dracut, systemd-container, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: git, btrbk, distro-info-data
Conflicts: initramfs-tools
Description: Freshroot — btrfs snapshot-based immutable root
 Makes a Linux installation effectively immutable by booting from
 read-only btrfs snapshots. A dracut initramfs module creates a writable
 clone at boot, and a staging pipeline handles updates via systemd-nspawn.
 .
 Includes:
  - dracut module for boot-time snapshot cloning
  - GRUB hook for snapshot-based boot entries, grouped by lineage
  - freshroot-update script for staged apt updates and custom scripts
  - freshroot-build script for two-tier "from scratch" snapshot builds
  - freshroot-install script for installing other OS releases as new
    snapshot lineages (each with its own retention quota)
 .
 The autoinstall bootstrap script (freshroot-setup) ships
 separately and is run from the installation media.
